-- title:
--   A uniform tame generator of inertia above q
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ and $L$ be fields with $L$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero and a $k$-algebra, with $L/k$ Galois, and assume every element of $L$ is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $q$ be a prime number and let $P$ be a valuation subring of $L$ satisfying `LiesOverPrime q`, that is, the image of $q$ in $L$ lies in the set of nonunits of $P$. Write $I_P$ for `P.inertiaSubgroupIn k`, the subgroup of $L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[k]} L$ obtained as the image of the inertia subgroup of $P$ under the inclusion of the decomposition subgroup of $P$ into the group of $k$-algebra automorphisms of $L$. The assertion is that there exists a single $\gamma \in I_P$ with the following uniform property: for every prime number $p \neq q$, every natural number $m$, and every $\tau \in I_P$, there are a natural number $j$ and elements $x, w \in I_P$ with $\tau = \gamma^{j}\, x^{p^{m}}\, w^{p^{m}}$. Thus one element $\gamma$ of $I_P$ generates $I_P$ modulo $p^m$-th powers simultaneously for all $p \neq q$ and all $m$.
--
--   This records, in the form needed later, the pro-cyclicity of tame inertia together with the fact that wild inertia at a place above $q$ is pro-$q$: modulo $p^{m}$-th powers ($p \neq q$) the whole inertia group is generated by one element, uniformly in $p$ and $m$. It feeds the variant [`ValuationSubring.exists_forall_tame_generator_inertiaSubgroupIn_of_forall_apply_algebraMap_eq`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_forall_tame_generator_inertiaSubgroupIn_of_forall_apply_algebraMap_eq), and the divisibility of the radical-fixing part of inertia is supplied by [`ValuationSubring.exists_mem_inertiaSubgroupIn_pow_eq_of_forall_apply_eq_of_isGalois`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_mem_inertiaSubgroupIn_pow_eq_of_forall_apply_eq_of_isGalois).
